                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1][b]Sphere Frustration\t\t* 6/10[/b][/h1]\n\nKeeping things simple and revisiting in a modern key. That's what Sphere Frustration does as  essentially uses PacMan's mechanics with a more modern design.\n\n[h1][i]INTRO & GAMEPLAY. What is Sphere Frustration about And how does it work?[/i][/h1]\nThe game is pretty simple. You are a ball, you roll around to collect a determined number of... Rocks I guess. Meanwhile a human is chasing you and if he/she reaches you it's game over. That's pacman essentially, but it's fine. There are a bunch of modes to play with:\n\nChallenge, where you collect rocks while 1 human chases you and another one collects the same stones, so first one who collects more wins. \nSurvival, you collect rocks while 1 human chases you. You must complete each map without being ever caught otherwise you start from the beginning.\nQuick game where you can play any level freely. With rocks to collect and a human chasing you of course, but this time you choose the map.\nSplit Screen Mode to challenge a friend sharing a keyboard or using gamepads.\n\n[h1][i]GRAPHIC. Engine And Artistic aspects.[/i][/h1]\nSphere frustration uses Unity. It has a very simple look, design and detail quality so it doesn't have high specs requirements and runs smoothly even on my laptop.\n\n[h1][i]SOUNDTRACK. Themes and Accompaniments.[/i][/h1]\nMusic is mainly made of catchy tunes with some clean guitar, something pop and simple I'd say. The only bad side about this is not about the kind nr the quality of the music used in game, but the fact that each stage has the same song. The game could have used at least two or three tracks more to play randomly and prevent that sense of repetitiveness that sooner or later comes after a while.\n\n[h1][i]LAST NOTES. What doesn't work?[/i][/h1]\nGame's title hints already at its frustrating nature, so the game's obviously based on learning the maps and practicing to succeed. \nThe game is fine in its ideas and mechanics, the real challenge (besides the brief challenge mode, obviously) is to finish the survival mode but the way the game is presented doesn't show itself in as an improving challenge. I mean, to complete the survival mode you need experience, know the map. That's why quick game allows you to play each map. But is there any point in having all maps available right from the beginning? Maybe it would feel more rewarding and challenging if each map was unlocked after completing the previous one. Or after you reach it in survival mode, so you have a reason to practice it with quick game then get back on survival again.\nAlso, just like pacman you could be able to gain the ability to face against the human. Who knows a randomly spawned bonus or frustration token that gives the ability to jump on the human's head to make it faint for x seconds, Don't know...\n\n[h1][i]TL;DR. Pros And Cons[/i][/h1]\n[h1]+++PROs+++[/h1][list]\n[*][b] MODERN PACMAN.[/b] The game can entertain as it's basically pacman. Who doesn't love pacman?\n[/list]\n[h1]---CONs---[/h1][list]\n[*][b] UNLOCKED.[/b] Every map is already available for quick play, it doesn't give a reason to play more this way as opposed with a system where you should unlock each map by completing the previous one or something like that.\n[*][b] ROOM TO IMPROVE.[/b] There's room for the game to improve, it could give more and explore its possibilities by expanding its gameplay maybe with bonus and variations besides the frustration tokens. And maybe some more audio tracks could help as well.\n[/list]\n\n[i]I played this game on this machine:\nLaptop Lenovo Z50\nIntel Core i5-4210U\n8Gb RAM DDR3\nGeForce 840M/Intel HD Graphics 4400\nWindows 10 Home x64[/i]\n\n[quote] You can follow my reviews through my curator page: [url=store.steampowered.com/curator/28510673]Everybody's reviews[/url]\nYou can also join my Steam group: [url=steamcommunity.com/groups/EverybodysReviews]Everybody's reviews[/url]\nYou are welcome to join and post your own reviews, we can support each other![/quote]",
